>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SLOW_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.SLOW_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by a less committing depth-first classical search.

`SLOW_TAC thms` safely saturates the state and then searches the first open
goal. Unlike `FAST_TAC`, it retains unsafe-rule alternatives even when an
instantiating rule is applicable. This can find proofs hidden by the fast
cascade, at the cost of a larger search. Dynamic pruning discards choices
that cannot affect remaining goals. There is no numeric depth or node
bound, so search can diverge.

The theorem list modifies the current classical rule set for this call.
The markers `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`, `SDest`, `Dest` and `Del`
add or remove rules. Every unmarked theorem is inserted as an assumption
before search starts. Content-bearing generic simplifier wrappers are
unwrapped and inserted; inert generic controls are ignored. Changes are
local to the call.

This tactic succeeds only with a complete proof; it never returns residual
goals.

### Failure

Fails if the search is exhausted without a proof, or if a found proof
cannot be replayed. It can diverge rather than fail. Malformed extra rules
can also cause failure during marker processing.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem slow_tac_example:
  (p ==> q) ==> (~q ==> ~p)
Proof
  classicalLib.SLOW_TAC []
QED
```

